  "honest_framing_note": "Wf-146 v2 / Wf-194 per-metal single-task chemprop v2 sweep (25/25 ok runs in 32.91 min).  hidden_dim=300, depth=3 (chemprop v2 default backbone, matches TODO-154 in-domain protocol); Adam(lr=0.001); 50 epochs; 80/20 stratified holdout per metal; BF16 autocast on encoder forward + fp32 head + BCEWithLogitsLoss; num_workers=4.  NO multi-task scaffolding, NO shared encoder across metals, NO per-metal heads, NO coord head, NO Wasserstein transfer, NO L2 guard, NO Noam scheduler, NO LR scheduler (plain Adam proved more stable in this single-task per-metal protocol than the v1 Noam scheduler that locked chemprop v2 BCE near 0.69 forever \u2014 see TODO-170 \u00a73.4).  Per-metal single-task design collapses to one independent BinaryClassificationFFN per metal.  Cross-metal LOMO transfer is intentionally NOT measured here (the per-metal design has no metal identity leakage from the held-out fold \u2014 there is no 'LOMO' experimental arm left to run).  The reported per-metal in-domain test_auc is the honest apples-to-apples single-task baseline; cross-metal transfer (e.g. via a learned shared encoder + metal-conditioned head) is a follow-up TODO-170 \u00a75 v3 (TODO-pending).",
